    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27SoEhAWhjW5v1h3ikkMniV)_\n\n## Summary\nNew module `sp-vulpea-convert-keywords` (section of `docs/tangles/vulpea/sp-vulpea.org`, required by `sp-vulpea-ext`), the sibling of `sp-vulpea-convert-properties` for file-header keywords.\n\n- `M-x sp-vulpea-convert-keywords` lists every `#+key:` in the first section of the current note, with how many notes use it and an example value, and you pick several (`completing-read-multiple`). `C-u` (or `sp-vulpea-convert-keywords-all-notes`) scans every Vulpea note and counts across all of them.\n- `#+title:` and `#+date:` are ignored by default (`sp-vulpea-convert-keywords-ignore`).\n- A preview buffer shows each note and the `- key :: value` lines it gets; nothing is written until you confirm.\n- The meta lines go after the header and drawer, join an existing meta block, repeated keywords become repeated lines, and a re-run adds nothing.\n- `sp-vulpea-convert-keywords-remove-original` (default `t`, like the property converter) removes the `#+key:` line.\n- The current note is left unsaved (`C-/` undoes); the all-notes run saves each file and skips ones with unsaved changes.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 8 ERT tests (`tests/sp-vulpea-convert-keywords-test.el`) in Emacs 29.3 batch; byte-compiles clean.\n- [x] Interactive flow and the all-notes path driven in batch with stubbed prompts and a stubbed `vulpea-db-query` on two temp files.\n- [ ] Try `M-x sp-vulpea-convert-keywords` on a real note with `#+bib-project:`, then `C-u` in the real vault (commit the notes first).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBPPHfzgLTkNeDC4q4)_",
